      93→```
      94→
      95→## 7. Pass/Fail Criteria
      96→
      97→### All tests PASS when:
      98→1. `go build ./...` completes without errors
      99→2. `go vet ./...` completes without warnings
     100→3. `go test -timeout 5m -race ./...` all pass (12/12 tests)
     101→4. E2E scripts exist and are executable
     102→5. `screenshots/` directory exists with `.gitkeep`
     103→
     104→### Any test FAIL when:
     105→1. Build fails
     106→2. Vet reports issues
     107→3. Any test fails
     108→4. Race detector finds data races
     109→
     110→## 8. Test Execution Summary
     111→
     112→- **Total Unit Tests**: 12
     113→- **Build Checks**: 2 (build, vet)
     114→- **Race Detection**: 1
     115→- **E2E Scripts**: 2 (e2e-screenshot.sh, asciinema.sh)
     116→
     117→All tests must PASS for this feature to be considered complete.
     118→
     119→## 9. Event-Driven Architecture Validation
     120→
     121→### Input Handling
     122→- Uses `termbox.PollEvent()` for blocking event-driven input
     123→- No background goroutine for input handling
     124→- Main loop handles all events synchronously
     125→
     126→### Game Restart Flow
     127→1. Game over detected in `Update()`
     128→2. `setGameOver(true)` called
     129→3. Main loop enters restart-wait loop (lines 186-197)
     130→4. User presses R → `reset()` called → game restarts
     131→5. User presses Esc/Ctrl+C → function returns, game exits
     132→
     133→This flow has no goroutine lifecycle issues because no input goroutine exists.
